# pb-deployer environment variables (copy to .env and adjust as needed)
# All are optional — the defaults are the secure/quiet choice.

# Required by SSH auth: path to the running ssh-agent socket. Usually already
# set in your shell (`eval $(ssh-agent) && ssh-add`).
# SSH_AUTH_SOCK=/run/user/1000/keyring/ssh

# Verbose [AUTH] host-key debug logging during SSH connections. Off by default.
# PB_DEPLOYER_SSH_DEBUG=1

# Opt into insecure SSH host-key verification. OFF by default — leaving it off
# keeps MITM protection: unknown host keys are still pinned on first connect
# (TOFU), but a *changed* host key fails the connection instead of being
# silently accepted. Only enable for throwaway/dev servers you trust.
# PB_DEPLOYER_INSECURE_SSH=1

# General debug logging for the logger package. Off by default.
# DEBUG=1
